#X obj 653 11 chaos.gbman0;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 452 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 A non-interpolating chaotic generator based on the Gingerbreadman
map \, a two-dimensional discrete dynamical system. Unlike interpolating
generators that produce a continuous stream of values between two consecutive
points \, this generator advances the map by one discrete step per
incoming bang.;
#X text 240 184 The map is defined by the difference equations:;
#X text 240 209 x(n+1) = 1 - y(n) + |x(n)|;
#X text 240 234 y(n+1) = x(n);
#X text 240 259 For most initial values (x \, y) the sequence of points
(x(n) \, y(n)) traces a bounded \, non-repeating orbit with a characteristic
"gingerbread man" shape. Typical initial values that put the generator
into the chaotic region are x = 1.2 and y = 2.1 (the defaults). The
output values are typically in the range of roughly -1.5 to 3.5 for
x and -1.5 to 3.5 for y \, but the exact bounds depend on the initial
values.;
#X text 240 390 The two outlets output the current x and y coordinates.
Because the values are not interpolated \, when the generator is driven
by a slow metro the output jumps between discrete points — this makes
the object useful as a source of stepped \, chaotic control signals
(for example \, for driving filters \, pan positions or pitches).;
#X obj 240 494 ui.link @background_color 0.90196 0.90196 0.90196
@title wiki: Gingerbreadman map @url
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gingerbreadman_map;
